WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.152 --> 00:00:03.011
- Good morning Believe Nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael,

00:00:03.011 --> 00:00:06.190
my one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.778
are going to solve all of
the world's major problems.

00:00:09.778 --> 00:00:12.470
So to help you on your journey,
today we're going to learn

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:15.661
how to brace yourself for struggle.

00:00:15.661 --> 00:00:17.177
Over to you LeCrae.

00:00:17.177 --> 00:00:19.531
(rooster crows)

00:00:19.531 --> 00:00:22.210
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.128
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:25.128 --> 00:00:29.014
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:29.014 --> 00:00:30.511
- I would tell myself, man to

00:00:30.511 --> 00:00:33.249
brace yourself for real
struggle, for real pain,

00:00:33.249 --> 00:00:36.245
for death, for loss, for hurt.

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:40.415
And then as an artist, I
would tell myself what I say,

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:41.594
I put it on the back of the book too,

00:00:41.594 --> 00:00:43.103
if you live for people's acceptance,

00:00:43.103 --> 00:00:44.663
you'll die from their rejection.

00:00:44.663 --> 00:00:46.460
And that's what I would
tell people because

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.986
tell myself, because I was so
worried about being accepted.

00:00:49.986 --> 00:00:52.520
These people to accept me,
these people to accept me.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.419
And, when they don't you
die, you crumble inside,

00:00:55.419 --> 00:00:57.940
you devastated but, if you
already know who you are,

00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.865
I feel like I'm made in God's image.

00:00:59.865 --> 00:01:03.228
My worth and value cannot be tainted.

00:01:03.228 --> 00:01:06.345
You can't add to my worth,
you can't take away from it.

00:01:06.345 --> 00:01:07.699
I was born with it,

00:01:07.699 --> 00:01:09.088
and so I don't have to
fight for your approval

00:01:09.088 --> 00:01:10.723
or your acceptance and I
would want my younger self

00:01:10.723 --> 00:01:14.186
to know that, be confident
in who God made me to be

00:01:14.186 --> 00:01:15.825
and be the best me I could be.

00:01:15.825 --> 00:01:17.565
- So starting a business is
one of the hardest things

00:01:17.565 --> 00:01:19.321
you will ever do in your life.

00:01:19.321 --> 00:01:21.077
People think it's going to be easy,

00:01:21.077 --> 00:01:22.627
but it's one of the hardest things

00:01:22.627 --> 00:01:23.850
you will ever do in your life,

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.143
no matter how hard you
think it's going to be,

00:01:26.143 --> 00:01:27.684
no matter how many videos you watch

00:01:27.684 --> 00:01:28.867
of people telling you it's difficult,

00:01:28.867 --> 00:01:31.934
it's still way harder and way worse

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:34.165
than what you thought it was going to be.

00:01:34.165 --> 00:01:35.093
It just is.

00:01:35.093 --> 00:01:36.579
That's life as an entrepreneur.

00:01:36.579 --> 00:01:38.776
People will judge you,
people will criticize you,

00:01:38.776 --> 00:01:40.114
people will hate on you.

00:01:40.114 --> 00:01:42.487
You'll run out of cash faster
than you thought you would.

00:01:42.487 --> 00:01:44.155
Customers aren't going
to come through the door

00:01:44.155 --> 00:01:45.443
like you thought they would.

00:01:45.443 --> 00:01:47.728
The media's not going to cover
you like you thought they would.

00:01:47.728 --> 00:01:49.484
Your social media campaign's
aren't going to take off

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:50.595
like you thought you would.

00:01:50.595 --> 00:01:54.442
Basically, if you take
whatever idea you had,

00:01:54.442 --> 00:01:57.477
and you have a best case, realistic case,

00:01:57.477 --> 00:02:00.457
worse case scenario, it's always way worse

00:02:00.457 --> 00:02:01.775
than your worse case scenario.

00:02:01.775 --> 00:02:04.825
That's just life as an entrepreneur
and I want to be realistic

00:02:04.825 --> 00:02:08.303
and share that because I really
struggled at the beginning

00:02:08.303 --> 00:02:10.227
and I wasn't prepared for it.

00:02:10.227 --> 00:02:13.408
I read magazine articles
and I saw documentaries

00:02:13.408 --> 00:02:16.620
of people who had successes
in entrepreneur and I thought,

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.845
I can do this, I can
be an entrepreneur too.

00:02:18.845 --> 00:02:21.566
And I was prepared to do the work.

00:02:21.566 --> 00:02:24.232
I didn't think it would
just be handed to me.

00:02:24.232 --> 00:02:27.870
But I wasn't prepared for how
low I would feel about myself.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:32.174
When I making $300 a month
and I was working and working

00:02:32.174 --> 00:02:34.199
and working and not getting any results,

00:02:34.199 --> 00:02:37.065
not getting any callbacks,
not getting any people buying

00:02:37.065 --> 00:02:39.849
and seeing so little traction,

00:02:39.849 --> 00:02:42.088
that I felt at that point,

00:02:42.088 --> 00:02:44.680
the lowest I've ever felt in my life.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.874
Because I knew anything
else that I worked on,

00:02:46.874 --> 00:02:50.937
I could get some results
with, at school or athletics.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.666
Whatever I worked on, it would improve

00:02:52.666 --> 00:02:56.044
and here I was working, and
I wasn't getting any results

00:02:56.044 --> 00:02:57.272
and I just felt so low.

00:02:57.272 --> 00:02:59.746
I felt worthless, I
felt like I had no value

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.713
and I actually told my
business partner that I quit,

00:03:02.713 --> 00:03:03.914
at one point.

00:03:03.914 --> 00:03:07.016
Because I just felt like I
needed to do something where I

00:03:07.016 --> 00:03:09.392
could feel like I'm
contributing something,

00:03:09.392 --> 00:03:10.943
because this just sucked.

00:03:10.943 --> 00:03:12.919
And I was too embarrassed and too ashamed

00:03:12.919 --> 00:03:15.419
to tell other people about it.

00:03:16.755 --> 00:03:19.666
My friends would ask me
come out to birthday parties

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:22.238
or beer night or anything
like that and I couldn't.

00:03:22.238 --> 00:03:25.145
I always had to say no
because I couldn't afford it.

00:03:25.145 --> 00:03:27.385
You know 20 dollars was
too expensive for me.

00:03:27.385 --> 00:03:29.646
And so I had to pick one thing
a month that I could go to,

00:03:29.646 --> 00:03:32.105
but I would never tell my
friends what was happening.

00:03:32.105 --> 00:03:33.775
I would always say that,

00:03:33.775 --> 00:03:35.476
I'm living the entrepreneur lifestyle.

00:03:35.476 --> 00:03:37.793
I'm just hustling hard on my business.

00:03:37.793 --> 00:03:41.212
I was too embarrassed to let
them know what the truth was.

00:03:41.212 --> 00:03:43.667
And so I think, part of
what I wanted to share

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:46.003
in this channel is showing the struggles

00:03:46.003 --> 00:03:47.664
that people go through to make it.

00:03:47.664 --> 00:03:49.756
That it often doesn't
happen in the first year

00:03:49.756 --> 00:03:51.545
or two years or three years.

00:03:51.545 --> 00:03:54.029
That you have to have a deep
passion for what you're doing,

00:03:54.029 --> 00:03:57.779
and just keep doing it and keep
doing it and keep doing it.

00:03:57.779 --> 00:04:00.500
And you do it because you enjoy the work.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.287
Because making YouTube
videos is fun for me.

00:04:03.287 --> 00:04:04.830
I enjoy being able to reach you guys,

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:07.919
whether I end up hitting
my million subscriber goal

00:04:07.919 --> 00:04:11.010
or other big goals that I have or not,

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.911
I enjoy doing the work.

00:04:12.911 --> 00:04:14.842
And so I think if you
really have a deep passion

00:04:14.842 --> 00:04:19.155
for what you're doing,
and expect to struggle,

00:04:19.155 --> 00:04:21.760
then you let yourself off
the hook a little bit,

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.569
just from an emotional point of view.

00:04:23.569 --> 00:04:27.093
That when you don't hit
the results, immediately,

00:04:27.093 --> 00:04:29.462
you don't beat yourself up
and feel worthless about it

00:04:29.462 --> 00:04:32.796
and you use that as motivation
to go off and do better.

00:04:32.796 --> 00:04:34.929
So the question of the
day today is I'm curious,

00:04:34.929 --> 00:04:37.717
what was the biggest surprise that you had

00:04:37.717 --> 00:04:38.550
as an entrepreneur?

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.483
Something that you weren't expecting

00:04:40.483 --> 00:04:42.442
but then that happened to you

00:04:42.442 --> 00:04:44.326
that you had to deal with
and struggle through.

00:04:44.326 --> 00:04:45.624
Really curious to find out.

00:04:45.624 --> 00:04:47.196
Share your story in the comments below.

00:04:47.196 --> 00:04:49.565
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Kelvin Scoon.

00:04:49.565 --> 00:04:51.659
Kelvin, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:04:51.659 --> 00:04:52.833
Your One Word.

00:04:52.833 --> 00:04:54.648
It really, really, really
means a lot to me man,

00:04:54.648 --> 00:04:56.429
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:58.981
So thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you.

00:04:58.981 --> 00:05:00.987
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:05:00.987 --> 00:05:03.256
and whatever your one word is,

00:05:03.256 --> 00:05:05.967
much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:05:05.967 --> 00:05:08.272
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:08.272 --> 00:05:10.817
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:10.817 --> 00:05:14.400
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:05:17.066 --> 00:05:18.512
- That the depth of anybody's struggle

00:05:18.512 --> 00:05:20.875
will determine the
height of their success.

00:05:20.875 --> 00:05:23.247
And I believe that everything
that I've gone through,

00:05:23.247 --> 00:05:25.405
in my whole life, you know,

00:05:25.405 --> 00:05:26.827
people ask me what you would change?

00:05:26.827 --> 00:05:28.436
I wouldn't change a thing, because

00:05:28.436 --> 00:05:29.761
everything that I've gone through

00:05:29.761 --> 00:05:31.888
has made me who I am today.

00:05:31.888 --> 00:05:36.532
You know, so I'm sitting here
very strong and very confident

00:05:36.532 --> 00:05:39.940
and got to love for a
lot of, lot of people.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.842
Jesus struggled and went through things.

00:05:41.842 --> 00:05:45.503
Everybody went through they own thing

00:05:45.503 --> 00:05:46.600
and people slandered them.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.195
I mean, I feel like if Jesus
can go what he went through,

00:05:49.195 --> 00:05:50.532
who am I?

00:05:50.532 --> 00:05:52.347
(laughs)

00:05:52.347 --> 00:05:55.612
I'm nobody, I'm just a
guy from the hood man,

00:05:55.612 --> 00:05:57.732
that just do this music, you know,

00:05:57.732 --> 00:05:59.303
but I'm just such a real person,

00:05:59.303 --> 00:06:01.457
I don't consider myself
a celebrity at all.

00:06:01.457 --> 00:06:04.189
I'm just so real and I love people that,

00:06:04.189 --> 00:06:06.275
you know man I just
flow through this thing

00:06:06.275 --> 00:06:08.227
and I let my music, I let God guide me,

00:06:08.227 --> 00:06:09.536
where he'd like me to go.

00:06:09.536 --> 00:06:11.690
But God ain't gon' just guide
you straight to success.

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:13.211
Not God.

00:06:13.211 --> 00:06:15.923
He gon' guide you through
a lot of mess, first.

00:06:15.923 --> 00:06:17.321
So that when you get the success,

00:06:17.321 --> 00:06:19.543
you know how to appreciate
it and you know how to

00:06:19.543 --> 00:06:22.743
stay with it and know
how to take care of it

00:06:22.743 --> 00:06:24.408
and that's called longevity.

00:06:24.408 --> 00:06:26.768
- My biggest challenge of this year,

00:06:26.768 --> 00:06:30.522
actually was convincing
members of my own team

00:06:30.522 --> 00:06:32.033
that this was a good call.

00:06:32.033 --> 00:06:34.053
I'd get kind of called in
front of a group of people

00:06:34.053 --> 00:06:36.480
who have known me and
worked with me for years

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:37.313
who would sit down and say,

00:06:37.313 --> 00:06:41.132
are you sure you want
to call the album 1989?

00:06:41.132 --> 00:06:42.872
We think it's a weird title.

00:06:42.872 --> 00:06:46.891
Are you sure that you want to
put an album cover out that has,

00:06:46.891 --> 00:06:48.722
less than half of you face on it?

00:06:48.722 --> 00:06:52.635
Are you positive, that you want to take

00:06:52.635 --> 00:06:56.103
a genre that you have
cemented yourself in,

00:06:56.103 --> 00:06:59.568
and completely switch to a new one that

00:06:59.568 --> 00:07:00.988
you are a newcomer to?

00:07:00.988 --> 00:07:03.621
And answering all those
questions with, yes I'm sure,

00:07:03.621 --> 00:07:05.476
that was I think something, that

00:07:05.476 --> 00:07:06.989
really frustrated me at the time,

00:07:06.989 --> 00:07:09.084
like guys don't you understand?

00:07:09.084 --> 00:07:12.611
I promise, this is what I'm dying to do.

00:07:12.611 --> 00:07:16.025
The biggest kind of struggle
turned into the biggest triumph

00:07:16.025 --> 00:07:17.159
when it worked out.

00:07:17.159 --> 00:07:20.742
- When I was seven and
a half, I was raped.

00:07:26.023 --> 00:07:29.856
I won't say severely
raped, all rape is sever.

00:07:35.706 --> 00:07:36.623
The rapist,

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:43.622
was a person very well known to my family.

00:07:43.622 --> 00:07:45.205
I was hospitalized.

00:07:49.959 --> 00:07:52.459
The rapist was let out of jail

00:07:54.363 --> 00:07:55.863
and was found dead

00:07:56.921 --> 00:08:00.051
that night, and the police suggested,

00:08:00.051 --> 00:08:03.468
that the rapist had been kicked to death.

00:08:05.064 --> 00:08:07.746
I was seven and a half.

00:08:07.746 --> 00:08:11.329
I thought that I had
caused the man's death

00:08:13.187 --> 00:08:15.687
because I had spoken his name.

00:08:18.362 --> 00:08:22.172
That was my seven and
a half year old logic.

00:08:22.172 --> 00:08:25.255
So I stopped talking, for five years.

00:08:28.629 --> 00:08:31.204
Now to show you again,

00:08:31.204 --> 00:08:34.204
how out of evil there can come good,

00:08:36.427 --> 00:08:40.245
in those five years, I read every book

00:08:40.245 --> 00:08:42.578
in the black school library.

00:08:44.609 --> 00:08:46.827
I read all the books I could get

00:08:46.827 --> 00:08:49.994
from the white school library.

00:08:49.994 --> 00:08:53.482
I memorized James Weldon
Johnson, Paul Laurence Dunbar,

00:08:53.482 --> 00:08:56.447
Countee Cullen and Langston Hughes.

00:08:56.447 --> 00:08:59.530
I memorized Shakespeare, whole plays,

00:09:01.527 --> 00:09:02.444
50 sonnets.

00:09:05.259 --> 00:09:08.926
I memorized Edgar Allen
Poe, all the poetry.

00:09:10.764 --> 00:09:12.993
Never having heard it.

00:09:12.993 --> 00:09:14.243
I memorized it.

00:09:15.396 --> 00:09:19.563
I had Longfellow, I had Guy
de Maupassant, I had Balzac.

00:09:23.248 --> 00:09:25.012
Rudyard Kipling.

00:09:25.012 --> 00:09:28.109
I mean it was Catholic kind of reading,

00:09:28.109 --> 00:09:30.526
and Catholic kind of storing.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:34.310
When I decided to speak,

00:09:35.674 --> 00:09:37.949
I had a lot to say,

00:09:37.949 --> 00:09:42.232
and many ways in which
to say what I had to say.

00:09:42.232 --> 00:09:45.007
I listened to the black minister,

00:09:45.007 --> 00:09:48.005
I listened to the melody of the preachers,

00:09:48.005 --> 00:09:50.177
and I could tell when they would start up

00:09:50.177 --> 00:09:52.115
♫ On that kind of thing,

00:09:52.115 --> 00:09:55.000
♫ When we didn't know they
mean to take our souls

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.481
♫ Straight to heaven

00:09:56.481 --> 00:10:00.010
or whether they meant to
dash us straight to hell,

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:02.024
I understood it.

00:10:02.024 --> 00:10:06.674
So out of this evil, which
was a dire kind of evil,

00:10:06.674 --> 00:10:11.016
because rape on the
body of a young person,

00:10:11.016 --> 00:10:14.433
more often than not, introduces cynicism.

00:10:16.246 --> 00:10:20.413
And there's nothing quite
so tragic, as a young cynic,

00:10:21.256 --> 00:10:24.994
because it means the person
has gone from knowing nothing

00:10:24.994 --> 00:10:26.744
to believing nothing.

00:10:27.595 --> 00:10:31.012
In my case, I was saved in that muteness,

00:10:32.197 --> 00:10:33.271
you see,

00:10:33.271 --> 00:10:35.938
in the sort of die, I was saved.

00:10:36.923 --> 00:10:40.423
And I was able to draw from human thought,

00:10:41.667 --> 00:10:45.176
human disappointments and triumphs,

00:10:45.176 --> 00:10:46.997
enough to triumph myself.

